{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_not_unital_of_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_not_unital_of_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L313-L322","doc":"**Contrapositive, the usable form.**  A `FrobeniusHopfData` whose object is\nnot a retract of the tensor unit has a **non-unital counit**: `ε(1) ≠ 1`.\n\nSo a non-trivial substrate is not merely \"not a bialgebra\" — its counit\nfails the most basic normalisation any coalgebra-with-unit is assumed to\nhave. That is the live question recorded in bean `qou-aawz`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.isoUnitOfUnital","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.isoUnitOfUnital","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L304-L311","doc":"**`A ≅ 𝟙_C`** from unitality of the counit alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_comp_unit_of_unital","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_comp_unit_of_unital","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L289-L302","doc":"**The substrate is the tensor unit as soon as its counit is unital.**\n\n`η ≫ ε = 𝟙` is `ε(1) = 1` — Mathlib's `BimonObj.one_counit`, and what any\nbialgebra or Hopf algebra assumes without comment.  Given it,\n`scalar_id_eq_counit_unit` reads `𝟙_A = η ∘ ε`, so `A` is a retract of\n`𝟙_C`; with the same hypothesis the other way round it is an isomorphism.\n\n**This needs no bimonoid comultiplication axiom.**  It is the antipode\naxiom (added 2026-09-14, bean `qou-c64q`) plus the Frobenius relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.scalar_id_eq_counit_unit_of_convolutionLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.scalar_id_eq_counit_unit_of_convolutionLeft","kind":"theorem","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L272-L287","doc":"**🛑 The substrate's own axioms force `ε(1)·𝟙_A = η ∘ ε`.**\n\nNo hypothesis beyond `FrobeniusHopfData`'s fields.  The right-hand side\nfactors through the tensor unit, so `𝟙_A` scaled by the scalar `η ≫ ε` of\n`End(𝟙_C)` factors through `𝟙_C`.\n\nRead in elements: `ε(1)·x = ε(x)·1` for every `x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.convolution_eq_left_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.convolution_eq_left_mul","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L257-L270","doc":"**The convolution `S * id` is left multiplication by a fixed element.**\n\n`(S * id) = (λ_A)⁻¹ ≫ (T ▷ A) ≫ μ` with `T = η ≫ (S * id) : 𝟙_C ⟶ A`.\n\nThis uses the Frobenius relation (via `comul_eq_frobenius`) and\nassociativity, and **no antipode axiom** — it is a statement about the\nconvolution, true whatever `S` is. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.convolution_reassoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.convolution_reassoc","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L248-L255","doc":"Pushing `S ▷ A` past a right multiplication, by **associativity of `μ`**.\nIn elements: `S(x₁)·(x₂·b) = (S(x₁)·x₂)·b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ConvolutionRight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ConvolutionRight","kind":"def","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L243-L246","doc":"**The right convolution condition.**  `Δ ≫ (A ◁ S) ≫ μ = ε ≫ η` —\nMathlib's `HopfObj.antipode_right`.  See `ConvolutionLeft`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ConvolutionLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.ConvolutionLeft","kind":"def","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L227-L241","doc":"**The left convolution condition, as a proposition rather than a field.**\n\n`Δ ≫ (S ▷ A) ≫ μ = ε ≫ η` — Mathlib's `HopfObj.antipode_left`, and what\n`FrobeniusHopfData` carried as a field between 2026-09-14 and 2026-09-15.\n\nIt is stated here as a `Prop` because the structure no longer carries it:\nit has **no non-trivial model over a field** (see\n`QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.FrobeniusHopfModelDichotomy`), and was\nreplaced by the anti-automorphism package on owner decision.\n\nNothing is lost by the move.  A hypothesis is strictly stronger than a\nfield: the theorems below now constrain **any** morphism satisfying this,\nrather than only a structure that declares it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.not_one_comul_of_nontrivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.not_one_comul_of_nontrivial","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L196-L206","doc":"**Contrapositive, which is the usable form.**  If the substrate object is\n*not* a retract of the tensor unit — i.e. `ε ≫ η ≠ 𝟙_A`, which is what\n\"the quantum vacuum is not the trivial object\" means — then the bimonoid\nunit axiom **fails**.\n\nSo the bialgebra compatibility is not an open option for this definition:\nit is excluded by the Frobenius relation together with non-triviality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.isoUnit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.isoUnit","kind":"def","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L183-L194","doc":"**`A ≅ 𝟙_C`.**  Adding the second unit-side bimonoid axiom\n`η ≫ ε = 𝟙` (Mathlib's `BimonObj.one_counit`) upgrades the retract to an\nisomorphism: the substrate object *is* the tensor unit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_comp_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.counit_comp_unit","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L166-L181","doc":"**The object collapses.**  `ε ≫ η = 𝟙_A`: the identity on `A` factors\nthrough the tensor unit, so `A` is a retract of `𝟙_C`.\n\nTogether with `comul_eq_of_one_comul` this is the whole content: the\ncounit law `Δ ≫ (A ◁ ε) = (ρ_A)⁻¹` cannot hold for the degenerate `Δ`\nunless every `x` equals `ε(x) · 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_eq_of_one_comul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_eq_of_one_comul","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L148-L164","doc":"**The comultiplication degenerates.**  Under the bimonoid unit axiom\n`Δ ∘ η = η ⊗ η`, the Frobenius relation forces `Δ = (λ_A)⁻¹ ≫ (η ▷ A)` —\nin elements, `Δ(x) = 1 ⊗ x`.\n\nThe hypothesis is Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.BimonObj.one_comul` written out:\nthe unit of the tensor-product monoid on `A ⊗ A` is `(λ_𝟙)⁻¹ ≫ (η ⊗ η)`,\nand unlike the `mul_comul` axiom it involves no braiding, so it is statable\nover a bare monoidal category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_eq_frobenius","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.comul_eq_frobenius","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L135-L144","doc":"Expanding `Δ = id ≫ Δ` through the left unit and then substituting the\nFrobenius relation.  No hypothesis beyond the structure's own axioms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unitor_unit_mul'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unitor_unit_mul'","kind":"theorem","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L130-L133","doc":"The same, right-associated, which is the shape `simp` normalises to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unitor_unit_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FrobeniusHopfData.unitor_unit_mul","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QuantumObservableUniverse/FrobeniusBialgebraCollapse.lean#L125-L128","doc":"`𝟙 ≅ 𝟙 ⊗ A --η ▷ A--> A ⊗ A --μ--> A` is the identity (left-associated). ","signatureChunk":0}]}